## Coordination

- Janitor **`DAY_CLOSE`** debt submits to the same coordinator (no sync zstd on janitor thread). See **`sync-timedb-archive-janitor-contract.mdc`**.
- **`run_scheduled_maintenance_pass`** with `reason=startup|every_n_chunks|ingest_queue_empty` must **submit** async DAY_CLOSE for **`eligible_deferred`** days (via `_submit_scheduled_day_close_from_snapshot`), not only log the candidate report. Report-only passes use other reason strings.
- **Supervisor delete handoff:** checkpoint-complete days at async manifest **`raw_delete_pending`** must not be re-submitted by startup discover, scheduled maintenance, or `_maybe_enqueue_immediate_day_close`; completion is supervisor **`reconcile_supervisor_raw_delete_pending`** → handoff or **`finalize_complete_if_filesystem`** via **`_apply_day_close_raw_removal_deletes`** (see **`sync-timedb-archive-janitor-contract.mdc`**).

## Manifest-fast handoff (`phase=done`)

When per-day raw removal manifest **`phase=done`**, handoff eligibility (`should_handoff_to_ingest`, `handoff_paths_for_ingest`, `_only_waiting_on_ingest_blocks_completion`, `discover_manifest_handoffs`, **`closed_raw_paths_on_disk`**, **`discover_closed_raw_on_disk_handoffs`**, **`has_closed_raw_on_disk`**) uses **manifest + `os.path.isfile`** only — **no** nested `build_remaining_raw_stats_by_daily_gz` full collect. This avoids OOM/stall on large archives when async manifest is stuck at **`raw_delete_pending`** but verify already finished, and unblocks boot **`startup_closed_raw_handoff`** recovery (e.g. 05-22 with hundreds of retryable skips on disk).

**Handoff allowed when:** at least one manifest path exists on disk and every on-disk manifest entry is a retryable skip (not verified / pending delete).

**Tar drop unchanged:** `try_finish_tar_drop_if_ready` and other filesystem gates still use `build_remaining_raw_for_daily_tar` with janitor accrual or startup snapshot when wired (`DayRawRemovalCoordinator.get_maintenance_snapshot` from supervisor).

**Unmanifested closed raw** may still exist on disk; handoff requeues known retryable manifest paths and defers async — tar drop stays blocked until filesystem truth clears (see **`sync-timedb-db-before-archive-contract.mdc`**).

